  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1103 AM MST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nRidging remains overhead keeping warm and dry conditions in the\nforecast. The tail end of a weak disturbance will bring some \nhigh clouds to the northern valleys this afternoon before \nspreading to the Divide mountains this evening. Looking on \nsatellite upstream these clouds are very diffuse...not a \nconcern. Some fog may occur overnight thanks to efficient\nradiational cooling but coverage doesn't look too widespread.\nSunny and dry conditions will also be the rule next week though\na quick shortwave may move through Tuesday night into Wednesday\nbringing a few showers to the higher terrain. There's hardly \nany available moisture so if this wave does pan out, minimal QPF\nis expected. High pressure then moves overhead to end out the \nweek with slightly above normal highs expected.",
